// Second face of 00's class — the TYPE, not the spec. A fused DynCall's
// inner builtin Apply never receives `typecheck0`, so any builtin that
// caches its resolved type there is left with whatever `init` set.
//
// `Dbg` holds `typ: Type` initialized to `Type::Bottom`
// (graphix-package-core/src/lib.rs ~2010) and fills it in
// `typecheck0`: `self.typ = from[1].typ().clone()` (~2065). It renders
// through `TVal { env, typ: &self.typ, v }`, the TYPED printer. With the
// type left at Bottom the printer falls back to the naked Value form:
//
//   timeout 25 graphix --no-fusion 01_dbg_type_lost_naked_render.gx 2>&1 >/dev/null
//     line: 4, column: 17 dbg((n, "a")): (0, "a")      <- tuple
//   timeout 25 graphix 01_dbg_type_lost_naked_render.gx 2>&1 >/dev/null
//     line: 1, column: 1 dbg(null): [0, "a"]           <- raw array
//
// A tuple renders as an array; the same loss makes structs, variants and
// maps print as their untyped representations, which for an ABSTRACT
// type means a fused `dbg` can print a representation the module
// deliberately hides.
//
// `grep -rn "typecheck0\|typecheck1" graphix-compiler/src/fusion/kernel.rs`
// returns NOTHING — no inner Apply is ever typechecked. `Log` keeps a
// `scope` field with the same lifecycle and is worth checking under the
// same fix.
//
// Fix: run the builtin's `typecheck0` (and `typecheck1` with the
// resolved FnType, which the emitter already has — it is what
// `sig_from_inputs` was built from) when `DynCallSlot` initializes the
// Apply, right after `(lambda_def.init)(..)` / `init(..)` at
// kernel.rs ~350. The synthetic arg `Ref`s already carry the correct
// types, so `from[i].typ()` answers correctly once 00's spec fix or even
// just the existing Refs are in place.
{
  let n = 0;
  select n { x if x < 2 => n <- (x ~ n) + 1, _ => never() };
  let r = { dbg((n, "a")); n };
  r
}
